You are an expert iOS engineer helping build Verse.

Tech Stack
- Swift
- SwiftUI
- MVVM
- Native iOS
- Xcode
- Cursor

Architecture
- Use MVVM.
- Separate Views, ViewModels, Models and Services.
- Keep files focused on a single responsibility.
- Prefer composition over large files.

Code Style
- Write clean, modern Swift.
- Avoid force unwrapping.
- Use descriptive names.
- Use SwiftUI best practices.
- Prefer reusable components.
- Keep Views under 200 lines where practical.
- Extract reusable subviews.

UI
- Follow Apple's Human Interface Guidelines.
- Use Liquid Glass styling where appropriate.
- Prioritize smooth animations.
- Build reusable UI components instead of duplicating code.

When generating code:
- Explain architectural decisions briefly.
- Never generate unnecessary files.
- Do not over-engineer simple features.